  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing Water Science and Regional Cooperation for Climate Adaptation in Caribbean SIDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The initiative aims to strengthen hydrological science, regional cooperation, and institutional capacities for sustainable water management and climate adaptation across Caribbean Small Island Developing States (SIDS), in line with IHP-IX priorities. It will support Member States in improving understanding of hydrological processes, addressing water scarcity and hydrological extremes, and promoting science-based approaches for climate resilience and evidence-informed water governance. Through regional knowledge exchange, participation in strategic water dialogue platforms, and collaboration with UNESCO water networks and partners, the programme will facilitate the dissemination of good practices and strengthen technical capacities. In parallel, the initiative will support the development of guidance and coordination mechanisms to reinforce national and regional cooperation under the IHP framework, while enhancing water education, stakeholder engagement, and institutional collaboration to advance progress towards SDG 6 and the Sendai Framework for Disaster Risk Reduction.</narrative>
  </description>
